## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: single `game` object; `mulberry32(seed)` used for map/trade/events/storms (no Math.random found); `endTurn()` calls updateProduction→updateColonists→updateCooldowns→checkAshstorm→updateTrade→fireEvent in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: 8x8 `this.map` built with `this.rng()`; `canBuild()` checks `tile.terrain !== btype.terrain`; `calcAdjacencyBonus()` sets `b.productivity`, read in `updateProduction()` as multiplier. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: `resourceCaps` enforced with overflow logging/clamping in `updateProduction()`; but only greenhouse has an input-consumption tie (water), no real ore→metal→parts chain (refinery declares `production.parts` with no metal draw). Score 1.

**F4 Population**: colonists have skill/skillLevel/fatigue/morale/assigned; `skillLevel` read in `updateProduction()` for `skillBonus`; `c.fatigue` never read by production code, only by `updateColonists()`. Score 1.

**F5 Needs**: `produced.food/water -= popConsumption` each turn; `handleShortage()` cuts morale; `moraleMult` feeds `updateProduction()`; unassigned colonists recover morale (+5/turn). Score 2.

**F6 Research**: 8 nodes with `prereq` checked in `canResearch()`, cost deducted in `doResearch()`; only farming_1/mining_1/water_1/storm_1/storage_1 have real effects read elsewhere — power_1, labor_1, automation are never checked anywhere else (dead). Score 1.

**F7 Events**: 10 entries in `eventDeck`, weighted pick in `fireEvent()`, cooldown via `eventCooldown`; only 3 events have choices (need 4+); all `effect: () => {...}` arrow functions reference `this.resources`/`this.colonists` but are defined at object-literal top level so `this`≠`game`, meaning `choice.effect()`/`event.effect()` throw and never mutate state. Score 1.

**F8 Trade**: `caravanPrices` computed from `globalDemand` (drifts via rng) and `this.resources[res]` (stockFactor); `caravanInventory` capped/decremented; `tradeWithCaravan()` handles both buy/sell, wired to click handlers. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `checkAshstorm()` fires with chance growing by turn, severity scales; damaged `b.health<100` reduces `productivity` in `updateProduction()`; `storm_1` research cuts damage 0.7x; `repairBuilding()` spends `parts`, restores health to 100. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: `saveToTextarea()` serializes full state to textarea; `loadFromTextarea()` does `JSON.parse` in try/catch with `alert('Failed to load save...')` on bad JSON, but no field-level content validation. Score 1.

**F11 End conditions**: win check in `endTurn()` (turn/pop/food/water thresholds); lose check in `updateColonists()` (`endGame(false,...)` at pop 0); `score` computed from pop/research/resources/turn; `end-game-modal` renders summary. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: tab buttons wired via `addEventListener`; `logEvent` stores `turn`, shown as `T{turn}` in `renderLog()`; tile tooltips show health/bonus; keydown handler for Space + digits 1-5; media queries at 768/480px. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (morale/fatigue range, storage caps, prereqs, worker exclusivity); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless turns calling core update fns and prints `computeStateHash()`, but it calls `this.fireEvent()` each iteration which will throw via the same `this`-binding bug, aborting the loop before restoring state. Score 1.

**G1 research→yield**: `researchDone.has('farming_1')`/`'mining_1'` checked via hardcoded per-building special cases in `updateProduction()`, not a generic effect-table read. Score 2.

**G2 shortfall→morale→output**: `produced.food/water` deficit → `handleShortage()`/direct checks cut `c.morale` → `avgMorale` → `moraleMult` multiplies `productivity` every turn, visible in header. Score 4.

**G3 storm→damage→loss→repair→recovery**: `checkAshstorm()` cuts `b.health` → `productivity *= b.health/100` → `repairBuilding()` spends `parts`, restores `health=100` fully. Score 4.

**G4 trade prices**: `caravanPrices` formula reads `globalDemand[res]` (drifts via rng) and `this.resources[res]` (stockFactor), recalculated every caravan visit. Score 4.

**G5 event choices mutate state**: `choice.effect()` writes intended `this.resources`/`this.colonists` changes, but arrow-function `this` is not `game` (top-level lexical scope), so the call throws and no state change ever actually lands; player sees no durable effect. Score 1.

